    {
      "@id": "item/download-reaches-the-browser",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 23,
      "name": "Download returns bytes the browser can actually fetch",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/74",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:10-user-facing-surface"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/files-actions-ui"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "The container smoke follows a Download link and asserts the bytes arrive and match the uploaded checksum -- that assertion is pushed FIRST and shown red against today's main, demonstrating the defect through the product's own harness before anything changes. A Decision records how the collision between spec 11 (bytes never pass through PHP) and spec 13 (one container, one port) is resolved, and names what the chosen option costs. The presigned host follows X-Forwarded-Host, so it does not break behind a reverse proxy the way it breaks on 127.0.0.1. The per-version download route added by item/files-versions-replace is covered by the same assertion.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-17T23:53:10Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T00:06:45Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/127"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/sqlite-immediate-transactions",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 24,
      "name": "Write transactions begin IMMEDIATE so busy_timeout can do its job",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/121",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:10-user-facing-surface"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "config/database.php states an IMMEDIATE transaction_mode rather than the skeleton's DEFERRED, so the write lock is taken at BEGIN and busy_timeout covers the queue worker's SELECT-then-UPDATE; the container smoke prints transaction_mode alongside journal_mode and busy_timeout, so a silent revert is visible in the log; and sqlite-busy-timeout-stated's why is corrected, since it currently cites the jobs-table lock as something the stated timeout already fixes. The suite cannot reach this at all -- QUEUE_CONNECTION is sync, per decision/0020 -- and the item says so rather than inventing a test.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T00:08:32Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T00:11:35Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/128"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/upload-silent-discard",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 25,
      "name": "Observe the silent upload discard, then give the operator recourse",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/106",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:10-user-facing-surface"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "doneWhen": "The container smoke carries request, requestfailed, response, console and pageerror listeners plus Livewire's upload events, and one instrumented run distinguishes the three bugs this has been treated as one of: never sent, sent and failed, or sent and answered with the state lost. Diagnosis is time-boxed to two CI rounds. Whether or not the cause is named, the operator gets recourse: a form that has not completed an upload within a stated interval re-enables its control and says so, instead of leaving a dead button with no error. If the cause is not named, it is filed as post-v1 with what the instrumented run did show.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T00:14:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T00:33:15Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/129"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/file-policy-trashed-file-guards",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 26,
      "name": "FilePolicy states, for every ability, whether an independently trashed file is refused",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/116",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:5-access-control"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/file-policy-null-directory",
        "item/files-versions-replace"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Every FilePolicy ability states its posture on a file trashed on its own in a LIVE directory, rather than three postures existing by accident: replace() refuses, update()/move()/legalHold() do not, and delete()/restore()/purge() deliberately must not. update(), move() and legalHold() refuse a trashed file; a FilePolicyTest case covers each; each carries a mutations.json entry. The reachability question is SETTLED rather than assumed -- a Livewire::test() case selects a file, trashes it out of band, calls renameFile() and asserts WHICH guard refused (403 from the policy, not 404 from a scoped restoration query), so the verdict says whether Livewire's restoration applies the SoftDeletingScope; that answer is recorded either way, because it is the same fact replace()'s guard rests on.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T00:47:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T01:06:00Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/135"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "item/files-three-pane",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 27,
      "name": "Tree sidebar rooted at the viewer reach, and a real breadcrumb",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/104",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:10-user-facing-surface"
      ],
      "size": "M",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/files-actions-ui"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "The sidebar renders Home first, then the viewer reach roots -- viewable directories whose parent is not viewable -- and their viewable descendants, asserted against the query: a grant on a nested directory alone makes that directory reachable from /files, written as a test that fails on main before the fix; the breadcrumb lists every ancestor the viewer may view and no others; collapse state is per-browser; the container smoke navigates two levels through the tree and asserts three breadcrumb items. FileBrowserTest keeps its unreachable-directory guarantees throughout. The LANDING PANE at /files, with no directory selected, lists the same reach roots as the sidebar rather than the true filesystem roots it lists today: Browser::render() filters on where('parent_id', $this->directory?->getKey()), which resolves to parent_id IS NULL, so a directory granted to the viewer whose parent is not viewable has a non-null parent_id and never appears there at all -- reachable only by typing its URL. That is issue 99, and without this clause an implementation could satisfy every other clause here and leave /files itself still broken for a nested grant.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T01:12:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T01:52:45Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/139"
      ]
    },
    {
