      "doneWhen": "Recents are filtered by DirectoryAccess so another user's file is absent; the page renders with zero data. Exactly one link on /files has the accessible name 'Home': spec 10 names BOTH the topbar entry and the sidebar's pinned entry 'Home', so the collision is the spec's rather than item/files-tree-sidebar's (issue #140). The sidebar entry keeps its visible text per the spec and carries an accessible name beginning with it ('Home directory'), so WCAG label-in-name holds; a test asserts the count of accessible-name matches and is shown failing against main first. Not renamed to the username (the tree's first entry already reads that) nor to 'My files' (a term the spec does not use).",
